NV_PK(21,{"do i need to order the duck ahead":"","how many people is one pot for":"","the cabbage is so soft":"","around the winter solstice each year schools of grey mullet swim to the southwest coast of taiwan fishermen call them black gold because the roe inside the female fish is worth a lot of money":"","the roe is taken out salted pressed flat and dried in the sun this is mullet roe or wuyuzi it is a beautiful golden orange like a piece of amber":"","to eat it you wipe it with rice wine grill it until the surface starts to bubble and slice it thinly eat it with a slice of white radish and garlic greens it is a fine dish for the lunar new year and banquets and you can try it at a hsia in tainan and shin yeh in taipei":"","in japan mullet roe is called karasumi because its shape looks like a stick of ink":"","is this mullet roe grilled":"","it is salty and rich":"","four herb soup":"","1 large chinese cabbage":"","2 pieces of dried flatfish":"","catch the ingredients for four herb soup":"","300 g pork intestine or pork stomach":"","1 pack of four herb mix poria fox nuts lotus seeds chinese yam":"","3 tbsp job's tears":"","wash the pork intestine very well with flour and salt":"","boil the pork for five minutes and cut it into short pieces":"","put the pork and the herbs into a pot of water":"","simmer for ninety minutes until the pork is soft":""});